     "body": "<p>I believe this is still working correctly, and that this IT would fail if it wasn't: <a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/fcrepo-http-api/src/test/java/org/fcrepo/integration/http/api/FedoraLdpIT.java#L1561\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/fcrepo-http-api/src/test/java/org/fcrepo/integration/http/api/FedoraLdpIT.java#L1561</a> — and I just tested a fresh build of master and found that I could populate the filename using Content-Disposition, e.g.:</p>\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">\r\n$ curl -X PUT -H <span class=\"code-quote\">\"Content-Disposition: inline; filename=\\\"</span>foo.txt\\<span class=\"code-quote\">\"\" -d \"</span>foo<span class=\"code-quote\">\" -H \"</span>Content-type: text/plain<span class=\"code-quote\">\" -H \"</span>Link: &lt;http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//www.w3.org/ns/ldp#NonRDFSource&gt;; rel=\\<span class=\"code-quote\">\"type\\\"</span>\" http://localhost:8080/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/file2</span>\r\n</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>Are you seeing something different? Is the issue that if no Content-Disposition header is supplied, that there is a blank filename?</p>",
     "created": "18/Sep/17 10:45 AM",
     "id": "19350",
     "jsdPublic": true,
